{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11220-q-a","id":11220,"title":"Q&A","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-15T06:28:38-08:00","id":11220,"title":"Q&A","content":"As we have quite a few threads now that are asking questions and get them answered I'm going to gather all the questions and answers into one general thread (hopefully less confusing that way).<br /> <br /> If you have questions, please use the other threads there (but send me a pm when you get an answer so that I can put it into here in case I overlook the thread and/or the answer).<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">General</span></b><br /> <br /> <b>Reducing primum - </b>Mentioned multiple times in the rules but no rules to be found<ul><li>So far only one situation is known where demons can loose primum (no hard rules, only a described situation):<br /> If they are exposed too long to a facility they can loose primum<b> (page 373 of the corebook)</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><i>It is currently unknown, if there will be any further possibilities / situations where demons can loose primum.</i></span></li> </ul><br /> <b>Regaining Aether when changing into demonic form - </b>Does this also work with partial transformations or only full transformations?<ul><li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9573-a-couple-of-questions-regarding-demon-rules?p=9575#post9575\">This comes only into effect when you change into your full demonic form.</a></li> </ul><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Pacts</span></b><br /> <i>Source is the demon creating the pact, target is the 2nd participant of the pact (with whom the demon makes a pact,<br /> regarldess if its mortal, supernatural or another demon)</i><br /> <b>Pact breaking </b> - If a participant of a pact dies, does the pact get nullified?<ul><li>No it only gets voided, if the &quot;document&quot; onto which the pact was signed gets destroyed. <b><i> (page 293 of the corebook)</i></b></li> </ul><br /> <b>Pact breaking -</b> Does a soulpact or the death of the target void (former) pacts the source had with the target?<ul><li><i><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">No answer so far</span></i></li> </ul><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Gadgets</span></b><br /> <b>Can a Demon Create a Gadget without know the embed / eploit used in the gadget?</b><ul><li>No the demon needs to know the embed / exploit that he wants to put into the gadget<b><i> (according to comments on kickstarter)</i></b></li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Cover</span><br /> Buying additional covers at character</b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b> creation</b> - what is the cover rating of these ?</span><ul><li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/10558-buying-cover-at-character-creation?p=10581#post10581\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Every additional cover bought at character creation starts with a cover rating of 7.</span></a></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Does going into demonic form (full form) make changes to compromise rolls ?</b></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Yes, as you can't act &quot;out of character&quot; while in demonic form. <b><i> (strongly incilned in the core rules)</i></b></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\">All other compromise rolls and even going loud affect the last cover you were in before going into demonic form. <b><i>(strongly incilned in the core rules)</i></b></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Can you spend willpower on a compromise roll?</b></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11220-q-a?p=12841#post12841\">No</a></span></li> </ul><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Embeds</span></b><br /> <b>Freeze assets</b> - What is the range of this embed?<ul><li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11404-range-for-freeze-assets?p=13951#post13951\">Within line of sight or within general area (up to STs discretion even targets seen on TV could be a possible target).</a></li> </ul><br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Exploits</span></b><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"font-size:18px\">Forms</span></b><br /> <b>Rivet arm </b>- What are the ranges of the gun<ul><li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9573-a-couple-of-questions-regarding-demon-rules?p=10367#post10367\">20 / 40 / 80 (same as shotgun)</a> (not 100%)</li> </ul><br /> <br /> <b>Claws &amp; fangs</b> - Which skill is used there<ul><li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/9573-a-couple-of-questions-regarding-demon-rules?p=11190#post11190\">Brawl skill is used for these</a></li> </ul><br /> <b>Can clairvoyant sight help with teleportation (line of sight) ?</b><ul><li><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11220-q-a?p=12841#post12841\">GM discretion, but usually yes.</a></li> </ul><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":914,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","user":"Ryu","date":". 11-24-2013, 03:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T07:54:21-08:00","id":11277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11220-q-a#post11220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Pact breaking -</b> Does a soulpact or the death of a participant void former pacts with the other side?</div> </div> </div> </div>With the other side? I'm having some trouble parsing this question. Do you mean with another Unchained?<br /> <br /> (Edit: Also, this is awesome! Thanks for putting it together!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelancer","edited":{"userid":17,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17-metrophelean","user":"Metrophelean","date":". 11-15-2013, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17-metrophelean","name":"Metrophelean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T08:48:28-08:00","id":11313,"title":"","content":"tnx rewrote that part and I'm using source and target now to differentate which side is meant","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T08:52:37-08:00","id":11314,"title":"","content":"Neat thread. But it would be even neater if you provided links to the posts (or quote from the book) that answered the questions, so we can see the answers for ourselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":508,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/508-sikker","user":"sikker","date":". 11-15-2013, 11:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/508-sikker","name":"sikker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T08:55:28-08:00","id":11316,"title":"","content":"Hmmm lets see (currently looking if/how I can get appropriate links together)....on that note anybody knowing if there is any limit to the size of a post?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T09:03:59-08:00","id":11324,"title":"","content":"The current post limit is 40 000 characters afaik.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/508-sikker","name":"sikker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar508_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-15T09:29:02-08:00","id":11344,"title":"","content":"ok that should be sufficient for some time <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T08:59:19-08:00","id":12100,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Does anyone know if subscribing to this thread will alert me when the OP is updated?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T09:27:04-08:00","id":12119,"title":"","content":"if this funtions like most other forums then nope.<br /> Btw if anyone sees any clarifications,... that I overlooked let me know (also in which thread) so that I can update this thread here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T10:13:01-08:00","id":12147,"title":"","content":"There are mentions in the Storytelling chapter that certain kinds of Facilities can drain away your Primum. It is a prelude to being reconnected to /recycled by the God-Machine. Some Integrators use them willingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T10:29:39-08:00","id":12169,"title":"","content":"Can you tell me which page?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T11:21:43-08:00","id":12193,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11220-q-a?p=12169#post12169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you tell me which page?</div> </div> </div> </div></span> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2022 Long-term exposure to a facility might reverse the Descent in a demon, removing dots of Primum. This could be intentional on the part of an Integrator, or the process of returning a captured demon back to his angelic state. Other demons may have strong reasons for interfering.<br /> <br /> &quot;Infrastructure and Techgnosis,&quot; page 372.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T13:26:18-08:00","id":12272,"title":"","content":"tnx (read it up. Interesting part).<br /> I've added it to the Q&amp;A.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":914,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","user":"Ryu","date":". 11-16-2013, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T23:07:12-08:00","id":12544,"title":"","content":"And now a question has entered my mind. Namely: Can restoration facilities be used to remove permanent glitches associated with High Primum? It seems to me the answer should be &quot;Doing that is like breaking one of a high-Psyche Sin-Eater's anchors, and so it would drop them down to a lower level of Primum.&quot; Or possibly &quot;No.&quot; But I'd like a clear answer from someone who knows better than I do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T02:39:59-08:00","id":12617,"title":"","content":"Couple of Questions.<br /> 1. If a Demon is Full Demonic form do they still need to act in character with their last cover are can they kill and murder without compromise rolls.<br /> 2. Can a Demon Create a Gadget without know the embed used in the gadget?<br /> 3. A Soul Pact can be made without the person knowing it very easily. You can rob a blood bank and then get someone to sign a paper with a pen full of their own blood. Get a job as Security at any place someone needs to Sign in then steal some of their blood by taking them out to drink drugging them. Next day they turn in to the job with a hang over you have them sign the pact when they sign in for work. Bam instant soul pact. Hell you can give them a bunch of stats just to get it to even out in willpower needed and then just grab them taking over their life on the spot. Considering this Do soulpacts need to be made with at least some form of foreknowledge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T02:47:30-08:00","id":12620,"title":"","content":"As for that first question, the text for the Extispicy Exploit would indicate that they don't need to act in-character anymore; some Demons prefer to go all Demonic to kill the animal necessary for this Exploit for this very reason, as it wouldn't be in-character for many Covers.<br /> Second question: from what I understand, nope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T03:26:42-08:00","id":12632,"title":"","content":"Hmmm I just looked. It is interesting that is the only place where I read that being in demonic form does coutner the &quot;acting out of character&quot; compromise rolls (although its logical it is not mentioned at the acting out of character part of the rules for compromise rolls). Are there any other such locations?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T05:39:47-08:00","id":12671,"title":"","content":"Not sure, but it makes sense to me. If you have several Covers, only the acts that are out of character for the Cover you're currently wearing would count. For example, if you have the identity of a high school kid, and the identity of a determined policeman, the only time you'll have to roll for Compromise when you shoot a criminal is when you're the high school kid, not when you're the policeman or your real Demon self. When you're wearing nothing but your Demonic form, there is nothing that would damage the credibility of <i>that</i> form (attracting the attention of Angels or the God-Machine is a whole other matter, though, and going full Demonic does trigger a nasty Compromise check, but <i>not</i> for acting out of character).<br /> There, the direct quote from Extispicy:<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Killing an animal (or a person, for that matter)<br /> to read its entrails might constitute a separate compromise if doing so would be grossly out of character<br /> for the demon\u2019s Cover. As such, some demons prefer to assume demonic form before gutting the<br /> sacrificial creature (the claws often make it easier anyway). </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T06:20:01-08:00","id":12691,"title":"","content":"Do check the Demonic Form Conditions, though - one of them says it happens when you kill someone in Demonic form. While you remain in demonic form with the condition on you get a penalty on social rolls due to no longer being able to identify with humans. (They're so very fragile...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/959-morkaischosen","name":"MorkaisChosen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"290"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T10:12:27-08:00","id":12788,"title":"","content":"Can you spend Willpower on a compromise roll?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T10:15:25-08:00","id":12790,"title":"","content":"If a Demon has Clairvoyant Sight, can it use that to qualify for the line of sight restriction for Teleporting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1178-ravenmancer","name":"Ravenmancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T10:24:31-08:00","id":12797,"title":"","content":"Each Incarnation is supposed to learn one class of Embeds more easily. Where does it say how that works? The Experience chart doesn't give a different cost for favored Embeds, which would be the logical place for the rule.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T10:50:14-08:00","id":12806,"title":"","content":"Incarnation doesn't actually have a strong influence over your acquisition of Embeds. At least one of your starting powers must be an Embed favored by your Incarnation, and when you go loud, you have access to any Embed that falls under that category. I believe that's it.<br /> <br /> Interesting thing about Demon, that its &quot;splats&quot; have relatively little mechanical heft behind them. I kind of like it, they mean enough about your character fluffwise that they don't need that mechanical reinforcement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T11:42:03-08:00","id":12841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11220-q-a?p=12788#post12788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you spend Willpower on a compromise roll?</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravenmancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11220-q-a?p=12790#post12790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Demon has Clairvoyant Sight, can it use that to qualify for the line of sight restriction for Teleporting?</div> </div> </div> </div>ST discretion. I would rule yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T17:28:41-08:00","id":13072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WalkingEye</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11220-q-a?p=12617#post12617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Can a Demon Create a Gadget without know the embed used in the gadget?</div> </div> </div> </div>I asked this question in the comments section of the kickstarter and matt said that the demon did need to know the embed/exploit in order to create the gadget. I asked the question about 4 days ago...its a long commentary thread.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Games - <a href=\"https://dust-and-shadow.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Dust and Shadow</a> (Vampire)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/626-darkfool","name":"DarkFool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar626_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T18:28:58-08:00","id":13095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravenmancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11220-q-a?p=12790#post12790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Demon has Clairvoyant Sight, can it use that to qualify for the line of sight restriction for Teleporting?</div> </div> </div> </div>I ruled yes in my game and it worked out just fine. Sure, it helped that the character was teleporting back to his apartment, but still, it didn't create any sort of silly situation or anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T21:54:20-08:00","id":13178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkFool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11220-q-a?p=13072#post13072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I asked this question in the comments section of the kickstarter and matt said that the demon did need to know the embed/exploit in order to create the gadget. I asked the question about 4 days ago...its a long commentary thread.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Can you give me a link to that answer? (on the right top of the post there is a #number that contains the link (example #25 for your post). tnx.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T01:14:36-08:00","id":13253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11220-q-a?p=13178#post13178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you give me a link to that answer? (on the right top of the post there is a #number that contains the link (example #25 for your post). tnx.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry it was in the comments section of the Demon Kickstarter. I can't see a way to link to that section of the Comments thread. You will have to go fishing for it I think around 4 days ago (now 5 days depending when you read this). <br /> <br /> Shaun Davis posted:@rose &amp; @matt - up to gadgets section. Does the demon need to know the embed or exploit that they want to make a gadget with?<br /> <br /> Matt posted back: @Shaun Davis: Yes.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Games - <a href=\"https://dust-and-shadow.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Dust and Shadow</a> (Vampire)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/626-darkfool","name":"DarkFool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar626_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"29"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T01:32:55-08:00","id":13260,"title":"","content":"Not an actual question but...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DtD, pg 54 under Inquisitors</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because gathering information can be a slow process, <b>Integrators</b> value their Covers.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T08:40:43-08:00","id":13410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkFool</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11220-q-a?p=13253#post13253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sorry it was in the comments section of the Demon Kickstarter. I can't see a way to link to that section of the Comments thread. You will have to go fishing for it I think around 4 days ago (now 5 days depending when you read this).<br /> <br /> Shaun Davis posted:@rose &amp; @matt - up to gadgets section. Does the demon need to know the embed or exploit that they want to make a gadget with?<br /> <br /> Matt posted back: @Shaun Davis: Yes.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps.</div> </div> </div> </div>tnx<br /> <br /> <br /> @ephsy: huh?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T09:07:20-08:00","id":13424,"title":"","content":"I think Ephsy is pointing out something that might've slipped past the editors' notice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T10:13:40-08:00","id":13474,"title":"","content":"@Ryu<br /> <br /> I asked these questions on another thread. If you think they're good questions, could you add them to the Q&amp;A?<br /> <br /> The exploit for Raise Dead p 259 indicates that demons use it in pacts with humans. Page 291 indicates that all benefits a demon can grant a mortal come from reality hacking that is automatically successful with the proper expenditures of willpower.<br /> <br /> Can demons resurrect family members through a pact without the Raise Dead exploit?<br /> <br /> Here's how I understand the rules so far: Giving a mortal a merit, healing damage, or removing persistent conditions (such as an illness), or increasing skills or attributes can be handled through the reality editing of the pact. Anything outside of that might require an embed or exploit.<br /> <br /> I would guess that a demon cannot grant immortality through any means that would add a major template to the mortal (Vampirism, etc), but the demon could do so by granting a merit based minor template, like as &quot;Thaumaturge&quot; or &quot;Psychic&quot;. Example: April asks the demon for immortality. The demon grants him the External Alchemy merit and tells David to start brewing immortality potions.<br /> <br /> Can pacts exist that don't involve reality hacking? Example: David Talbot (Mortal) doesn't just want to be immortal. He wants to be a Vampire, but since Louis (vampire) won't turn him, he goes to Asmodeus (demon) for help. Asmodeus can't mystically transform David into a vampire since the mystery of Vitae isn't in the demon's purview, but he's had amicable dealings with Lestat (vampire), so he calls in a favor and has David embraced to hold up his end of the pact.<br /> <br /> Last question: can a demon grant a mortal the ability to use an Embed without just giving the mortal a gadget? I ask because this is one of the things classic DTF demons could grant mortals in exchange for Faith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T17:26:33-08:00","id":14999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11220-q-a?p=13474#post13474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would guess that a demon cannot grant immortality through any means that would add a major template to the mortal (Vampirism, etc), but the demon could do so by granting a merit based minor template, like as &quot;Thaumaturge&quot; or &quot;Psychic&quot;. Example: April asks the demon for immortality. The demon grants him the External Alchemy merit and tells David to start brewing immortality potions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not familiar with the rules for that, but isn't it possible to create a Proximi with access to high-level anti-aging spells?<br /> <br /> I know you could easily pull this off if you're including <i>Genius: the Transgression</i> in your WoD, but I'm not as familiar with Mage's rules for this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T17:33:04-08:00","id":15004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11220-q-a?p=14999#post14999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not familiar with the rules for that, but isn't it possible to create a Proximi with access to high-level anti-aging spells?</div> </div> </div> </div>Such spells require Life 5; Proximus Blessings cut off at replicating four dot spells due to the extra dot a blessing adds to its Merit cost to replicate a rote.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T21:18:57-08:00","id":15106,"title":"","content":"Also, to create a Proximus, I believe you have to have access to the Archmaster template.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T04:28:10-08:00","id":17073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Octavo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11220-q-a?p=13474#post13474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Ryu<br /> <br /> I asked these questions on another thread. If you think they're good questions, could you add them to the Q&amp;A?<br /> <br /> The exploit for Raise Dead p 259 indicates that demons use it in pacts with humans. Page 291 indicates that all benefits a demon can grant a mortal come from reality hacking that is automatically successful with the proper expenditures of willpower.<br /> <br /> Can demons resurrect family members through a pact without the Raise Dead exploit?<br /> <br /> Here's how I understand the rules so far: Giving a mortal a merit, healing damage, or removing persistent conditions (such as an illness), or increasing skills or attributes can be handled through the reality editing of the pact. Anything outside of that might require an embed or exploit.<br /> <br /> I would guess that a demon cannot grant immortality through any means that would add a major template to the mortal (Vampirism, etc), but the demon could do so by granting a merit based minor template, like as &quot;Thaumaturge&quot; or &quot;Psychic&quot;. Example: April asks the demon for immortality. The demon grants him the External Alchemy merit and tells David to start brewing immortality potions.<br /> <br /> Can pacts exist that don't involve reality hacking? Example: David Talbot (Mortal) doesn't just want to be immortal. He wants to be a Vampire, but since Louis (vampire) won't turn him, he goes to Asmodeus (demon) for help. Asmodeus can't mystically transform David into a vampire since the mystery of Vitae isn't in the demon's purview, but he's had amicable dealings with Lestat (vampire), so he calls in a favor and has David embraced to hold up his end of the pact.<br /> <br /> Last question: can a demon grant a mortal the ability to use an Embed without just giving the mortal a gadget? I ask because this is one of the things classic DTF demons could grant mortals in exchange for Faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are any of the questions answered already? (if so can you pm me the links to them and the answers?) tnx","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T17:19:47-08:00","id":20877,"title":"","content":"Quick question about the Terrible form merit. To my understanding can a player only pick this merit max 4 times (once for body modification once per technological Advancement ect.) or can he buy modification over and over?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T21:34:56-08:00","id":20988,"title":"","content":"I view it like a fighting style merit, I'd rule just 4 times","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/991-pgolasze13","name":"pgolasze13","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-30T22:13:51-08:00","id":20999,"title":"","content":"A couple questions about Inflict Stigmata:<br /> <br /> 1) Do characters made stigmatic via the Exploit get the three dots of Supernatural Merits?<br /> 2) If so, can the demon determine how they're distributed and/or how the stigmata manifests?<br /> <br /> I've got a Guardian with an apocalypse cult who wants to make einherjar and Cursed and Biokinesis seem fitting, to give an example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T02:54:49-08:00","id":21077,"title":"","content":"Also something from my side. With the specialities: One must be chosen at char creation that is a possible breach of cover if ppl know the character has it.<br /> What is if the character has 2 (or 3) covers at startup? Must it be a breach for all covers or only for 1 (the &quot;maincover....or first cover&quot;)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/914-ryu","name":"Ryu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T03:16:25-08:00","id":21091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11220-q-a?p=21077#post21077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also something from my side. With the specialities: One must be chosen at char creation that is a possible breach of cover if ppl know the character has it.<br /> What is if the character has 2 (or 3) covers at startup? Must it be a breach for all covers or only for 1 (the &quot;maincover....or first cover&quot;)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it depends of the specialty.A Craft specialty in Butchery, taking the example from the book, can be a breach if the current Cover is that of a vegetarian. However, if at startup, that same Demon has a second Cover as, say, a chef or a hunter, then this is a perfectly reasonable specialty for them to have, and they're going to get a 2nd Specialty that may endanger this Cover, or at least that's how I'd do it.<br /> <br /> If the Specialty in question is something like Stigmatics or While On Fire, though, it's going to be strange for pretty much anybody to have, therefore it would suffice for your starting Cover(s). And any other you might get afterward, for that matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T09:22:00-08:00","id":21691,"title":"","content":"Just pick some that's bizarre for both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-02T22:42:38-08:00","id":22134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/11220-q-a?p=21077#post21077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also something from my side. With the specialities: One must be chosen at char creation that is a possible breach of cover if ppl know the character has it.<br /> What is if the character has 2 (or 3) covers at startup? Must it be a breach for all covers or only for 1 (the &quot;maincover....or first cover&quot;)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd just discuss it with the ST and pick something that makes sense. If you want to be all rules technical about it, you pick your specializations long before you select Merits (and thus is able to buy additional Covers) so by that token it doesn't make sense to keep anything other than the first Cover in mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/635-slaunyeh","name":"Slaunyeh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar635_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-04T18:44:30-08:00","id":23438,"title":"","content":"Question on warding do Demons add their Primum or cover or nothing to the presence occult roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1151-walkingeye","name":"WalkingEye","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1151_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}